/-
# Arithmetic on the Moebius Band: A Number System with a Twist

This file formalizes a "twisted" number system modeled on the geometry of the
Moebius band, viewed as the total space of the nontrivial real (here, integral)
line bundle over the circle.

## Physical / topological background

The Moebius band is the mapping torus of the orientation-reversing map `x ↦ -x`
on a fiber.  Concretely, take the strip `loop ∈ ℝ`, `height ∈ ℝ` and glue
`(loop, height) ~ (loop + 1, -height)`.  Travelling once around the core circle
(`loop ↦ loop + 1`) reverses the transverse direction: this is the **monodromy**
of the band, the algebraic shadow of the famous "twist".

We make this into an *arithmetic*: the **Moebius integers** `𝕄 = ℤ × ℤ`, where
`loop : ℤ` counts signed trips around the band and `height : ℤ` is the transverse
coordinate.  The group law encodes "walk, then walk again, carrying the twist":

    (p, h) * (q, k) = (p + q, h + twist(p) · k),      twist(p) = (-1)^p.

This is the semidirect product `ℤ ⋊ ℤ` with `ℤ` acting by sign monodromy — i.e.
the fundamental group of the Klein bottle, `⟨x, y | x y x⁻¹ = y⁻¹⟩`.  The twist
is exactly what makes this number system **non-commutative**, distinguishing it
from the flat cylinder `ℤ × ℤ`.

## Main results

* `Mob.instGroup` : `𝕄` is a group.
* `Mob.not_commutative` : the twist genuinely breaks commutativity.
* `Mob.moebius_relation` : the defining twist relation `x * y * x⁻¹ = y⁻¹`.
* `Mob.loopHom` : the projection to the core circle `ℤ` is a group homomorphism.
* `Mob.height_normal` : the transverse fiber `{(0, h)}` is a normal subgroup.
* `Mob.center_eq` : the center is `{(p, 0) : p even}` — the "untwisted, central"
  loops.
* `Mob.torsionFree` : `𝕄` is torsion-free (aspherical manifold ⇒ no torsion).

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
Hypothesis H1: the monodromy sign `twist p = (-1)^p` is a monoid hom `(ℤ,+) → (ℤˣ-like)`,
  i.e. `twist (p+q) = twist p * twist q`.  This is THE structural fact that powers
  associativity of the twisted product.  Verified below as `tsign_add`.
Hypothesis H2: the twist must make the system non-abelian (else it is just the
  cylinder).  Verified concretely via `not_commutative` with witnesses (1,0),(0,1).
Hypothesis H3 (failure-mode analysis): a naive "twist by height" law
  `(p,h)*(q,k) = (p+q, h + (-1)^k ...)` would FAIL associativity because the acting
  coordinate would not be additive.  The acting coordinate MUST be the loop `p`,
  matching that monodromy lives on the base circle, not the fiber.
-/
import Mathlib

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
-- Experimental log (cycle 1):
--  * Built 𝕄 = ℤ ⋊ ℤ with twist(p) = (-1)^p as a custom `structure Mob`.
--  * Outcome: the WHOLE group structure hinges on one identity, `tsign_add`
--    (twist is multiplicative). Once proved, mul_assoc fell out by `ring`.
--  * Insight: associativity of a semidirect product is equivalent to the
--    action being a homomorphism — the formalization makes this dependency
--    completely explicit (mul_assoc' literally `rw [tsign_add]; ring`).
--  * Non-abelianness verified constructively: (1,0)*(0,1)=(1,-1) but
--    (0,1)*(1,0)=(1,1); the twist is the unique source of this asymmetry.
--  * Center experiment: conjectured center = even-loop/zero-height; CONFIRMED
--    via `center_eq`. Probing with (0,1) forces tsign p = 1 (Even p); probing
--    with (1,0) forces 2h = 0 (h = 0). Two probes pin the center exactly.
--  * Torsion experiment: feared odd-loop elements might be torsion since
--    (p,h)^2 = (2p,0) collapses the height. FALSE ALARM — the loop coordinate
--    grows linearly (n·p), so order is infinite unless p=0, and then the fiber
--    is free. `torsionFree` confirms the band is aspherical-style torsion-free.
--  * Failure mode logged (see H3 in header): twisting by the FIBER coordinate
--    instead of the loop breaks associativity — the acting index must live on
--    the base circle. This is the formal fingerprint of "monodromy on S¹".
-- !-- end Lab Notes -- !--

namespace Physics.MoebiusArithmetic

/-! ## The monodromy sign (the "twist") -/

/-- The monodromy sign of the Moebius band: `+1` after an even number of trips,
    `-1` after an odd number.  Algebraically `(-1)^p`. -/
def tsign (p : ℤ) : ℤ := if Even p then 1 else -1

@[simp] lemma tsign_zero : tsign 0 = 1 := by
  decide +kernel

/-- The twist is multiplicative over loops: this is the monodromy homomorphism. -/
lemma tsign_add (p q : ℤ) : tsign (p + q) = tsign p * tsign q := by
  unfold tsign; by_cases hp : Even p <;> by_cases hq : Even q <;> simp +decide [ hp, hq, parity_simps ] ;

@[simp] lemma tsign_neg (p : ℤ) : tsign (-p) = tsign p := by
  unfold tsign; aesop;

@[simp] lemma tsign_mul_self (p : ℤ) : tsign p * tsign p = 1 := by
  unfold tsign; by_cases hp : Even p <;> simp +decide [ hp ] ;

lemma tsign_eq_one_or_neg_one (p : ℤ) : tsign p = 1 ∨ tsign p = -1 := by
  unfold tsign; by_cases hp : Even p <;> simp +decide [ hp ] ;

/-! ## The Moebius integers -/

/-- The Moebius integers `𝕄`: `loop` counts trips around the core circle,
    `height` is the transverse coordinate on the band. -/
structure Mob where
  /-- Number of signed trips around the core circle. -/
  loop : ℤ
  /-- Transverse coordinate across the band. -/
  height : ℤ
deriving DecidableEq

namespace Mob

@[ext] lemma ext' {a b : Mob} (hl : a.loop = b.loop) (hh : a.height = b.height) :
    a = b := by
  cases a; cases b; simp_all

/-- The twisted product: walk `p` loops, then `q` loops carrying the monodromy. -/
instance : Mul Mob := ⟨fun a b => ⟨a.loop + b.loop, a.height + tsign a.loop * b.height⟩⟩

instance : One Mob := ⟨⟨0, 0⟩⟩

instance : Inv Mob := ⟨fun a => ⟨-a.loop, -(tsign a.loop * a.height)⟩⟩

@[simp] lemma mul_loop (a b : Mob) : (a * b).loop = a.loop + b.loop := rfl
@[simp] lemma mul_height (a b : Mob) :
    (a * b).height = a.height + tsign a.loop * b.height := rfl
@[simp] lemma one_loop : (1 : Mob).loop = 0 := rfl
@[simp] lemma one_height : (1 : Mob).height = 0 := rfl
@[simp] lemma inv_loop (a : Mob) : a⁻¹.loop = -a.loop := rfl
@[simp] lemma inv_height (a : Mob) : a⁻¹.height = -(tsign a.loop * a.height) := rfl

lemma mul_assoc' (a b c : Mob) : a * b * c = a * (b * c) := by
  -- By definition of multiplication, we have:
  have h_mul_def : ∀ (a b : Mob), a * b = ⟨a.loop + b.loop, a.height + tsign a.loop * b.height⟩ := by
    aesop;
  simp +decide only [h_mul_def];
  rw [ tsign_add ] ; ring

lemma one_mul' (a : Mob) : 1 * a = a := by
  -- By definition of multiplication, we have $1 * a = ⟨0 + a.loop, 0 + tsign 0 * a.height⟩$.
  have h_mul : 1 * a = ⟨0 + a.loop, 0 + tsign 0 * a.height⟩ := by
    rfl;
  simp_all +decide [ tsign ]

lemma mul_one' (a : Mob) : a * 1 = a := by
  exact Mob.ext' ( by simp +decide [ Mob.mul_loop ] ) ( by simp +decide [ Mob.mul_height ] )

lemma inv_mul_cancel' (a : Mob) : a⁻¹ * a = 1 := by
  exact Mob.ext' ( by simp +decide [ Mob.mul_loop, Mob.inv_loop ] ) ( by simp +decide [ Mob.mul_height, Mob.inv_height, tsign_neg ] )

instance instGroup : Group Mob where
  mul_assoc := mul_assoc'
  one_mul := one_mul'
  mul_one := mul_one'
  inv_mul_cancel := inv_mul_cancel'

/-! ## The twist breaks commutativity -/

/-- The twist genuinely makes `𝕄` non-commutative: it is not the flat cylinder. -/
theorem not_commutative : ∃ a b : Mob, a * b ≠ b * a := by
  exists ⟨ 1, 0 ⟩, ⟨ 0, 1 ⟩

/-- The defining Moebius/Klein relation: conjugating a transverse element by one
    loop reverses it — `x y x⁻¹ = y⁻¹`.  This is the algebra of the twist. -/
theorem moebius_relation (h : ℤ) :
    (⟨1, 0⟩ : Mob) * ⟨0, h⟩ * (⟨1, 0⟩ : Mob)⁻¹ = ⟨0, -h⟩ := by
      ext <;> simp +decide [ mul_assoc ];
      unfold tsign; norm_num;

/-! ## The core circle: projection to the loop coordinate -/

/-- The band deformation-retracts to its core circle: the loop projection is a
    surjective group homomorphism `𝕄 → ℤ`. -/
def loopHom : Mob →* Multiplicative ℤ where
  toFun a := Multiplicative.ofAdd a.loop
  map_one' := rfl
  map_mul' a b := by
    simp only [mul_loop, ofAdd_add]

theorem loopHom_surjective : Function.Surjective loopHom := by
  intro x;
  exact ⟨ ⟨ Multiplicative.toAdd x, 0 ⟩, by rfl ⟩

/-! ## The transverse fiber is a normal subgroup -/

/-- The transverse fiber `{(0, h)}` — pure "across the band" motions. -/
def heightSubgroup : Subgroup Mob where
  carrier := {a | a.loop = 0}
  one_mem' := rfl
  mul_mem' {a b} ha hb := by
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, mul_loop] at *
    omega
  inv_mem' {a} ha := by
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, inv_loop] at *
    omega

/-
The transverse fiber is a normal subgroup (it is the kernel of `loopHom`).
-/
theorem height_normal : heightSubgroup.Normal := by
  constructor;
  simp +decide [ heightSubgroup, mul_assoc ]

theorem height_eq_ker : heightSubgroup = loopHom.ker := by
  ext a;
  simp +decide [ heightSubgroup, loopHom ]

/-- The transverse fiber is abelian, even though the whole band is not. -/
theorem height_comm (a b : Mob) (ha : a.loop = 0) (hb : b.loop = 0) :
    a * b = b * a := by
      convert Mob.ext' ?_ ?_ <;> simp +decide [ ha, hb, Mob.mul_loop, Mob.mul_height ];
      grind

/-! ## The center: untwisted central loops -/

/-
The center of `𝕄` is exactly the *even* loops with zero height: the motions
    that survive the monodromy unchanged.
-/
theorem center_eq :
    (Subgroup.center Mob : Set Mob) = {a | Even a.loop ∧ a.height = 0} := by
      -- To show that the center ofMob is exactly the set of even loops with zero height, we need to show two inclusions.
      ext a
      constructor
      all_goals generalize_proofs at *;
      · intro ha
        have h_even_loop : Even a.loop := by
          have h_tsign_p : tsign a.loop = 1 := by
            have := ha.comm ⟨ 0, 1 ⟩;
            replace := congr_arg Mob.height this; simp +decide [ Mob.mul_height ] at this;
            grind;
          unfold tsign at h_tsign_p; aesop;
        have h_zero_height : a.height = 0 := by
          have := ha.comm ⟨ 1, 0 ⟩;
          have := congr_arg Mob.height this; norm_num [ Mob.mul_height, Mob.mul_loop ] at this;
          unfold tsign at this; norm_num at this; linarith;
        exact ⟨h_even_loop, h_zero_height⟩;
      · intro ha
        rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
        intro g
        exact Mob.ext'
          (by simp [Mob.mul_loop]; omega)
          (by simp [ha.1, ha.2, Mob.mul_height, tsign])

/-! ## Torsion-freeness: the band carries no finite cycles -/

/-- `𝕄` is torsion-free: no nontrivial element has finite order.  (The Moebius
    band is aspherical, so its symmetry arithmetic has no torsion.) -/
theorem torsionFree (a : Mob) (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) (h : a ^ n = 1) : a = 1 := by
  -- Let us show that $(a^n).loop = n \cdot a.loop$.
  have h_loop_mul : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : Mob), (a^n).loop = n * a.loop := by
    intro n a; induction n <;> simp_all +decide [ pow_succ, add_mul ] ;
  -- By induction on $n$, we can show that $(a^n).height = n \cdot a.height$ if $a.loop = 0$.
  have h_height_mul : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : Mob), a.loop = 0 → (a^n).height = n * a.height := by
    intro n a ha; induction n <;> simp_all +decide [ pow_succ, add_mul ] ;
  -- By definition of $a^n$, we know that $(a^n).loop = n \cdot a.loop$ and $(a^n).height = n \cdot a.height$ if $a.loop = 0$.
  have h_loop : a.loop = 0 := by
    specialize h_loop_mul n a; aesop;
  have h_height : a.height = 0 := by
    specialize h_height_mul n a h_loop; replace h := congr_arg Mob.height h; aesop;
  exact Mob.ext' ( by simp +decide [ h_loop ] ) ( by simp +decide [ h_height ] )

end Mob

end Physics.MoebiusArithmetic